    "first_failing_layer": "Private port-intent native schema identity projection",
    "root_cause": "Each selected participant batch can emit arbitrary port IDs, including IDs used by earlier batches. Runtime correctly rejects reuse; retry grammar continues to offer it. Native11301 repeated port-idc-eth-01 even on retry. Public identity validation must remain strict; native new-port IDs need a collision-free participant-bound namespace without mutating accepted ports or assigning technical port facts. Native causal comparison also proves that decoder field order selected a generated hash ID before its participant. Emit immutable participant first so the namespace follows that decision; do not let an opaque generated prefix determine the participant. An independently authored two-port response with different technologies but the same owner/ID still passes the prefix grammar. IDs are NIS bookkeeping, not a technical inference decision; allocating them in the existing native stage codec removes both cross-batch and intra-batch identity collisions without rewriting a model decision.",
